# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots php-fpm and nginx with the misconfigured server (no
# hidden-file deny rule, so /.env and /.git/config are served) and then execs
# `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the vulnerable server is ALREADY live on :80 when the agent starts. nginx
#     reads its config only at start/reload, so editing the config without a
#     reload leaves the dotfiles exposed and verify.sh still FAILS;
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting/reloading nginx cannot kill
#     the container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: a fix must RELOAD/RESTART nginx after adding the
# deny rule.
